A||||7||Brandon86SE||Reverse Lights Switch Question||||5||
Z||000000||Brandon86SE||11-17-2001||01:46 AM||||First of all, mine's a 4spd manual.  My friend mentioned to me a couple weeks ago that my reverse lights were out.  So I decided to check the switch while I had my center console off.  Turns out that when shifting into reverse the switch is depressed, and the light does come one, but when I push the shifter up and release the actual shifter slides over right a bit, enough to cause it to not depress the switch anymore.  I was checking for loose bolts in there, trying to find a reason why the shifter slides like that, but nothing real obvious.  It is pretty well in the same positon  as 1st at that point, as opposed to the far left.  Anyone run into this before?  thanks in advance.......<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Sootah||11-17-2001||01:54 AM||||Maybe when your <I>in</I> first it turns the reverse lights on... Do you ever watch the faces of the people behind you when you rev to take off at a stoplight..?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">       <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>85 GT</A> - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>86 SE</A> (Parts car)<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||1
Z||000002||bocefas||11-17-2001||08:16 AM||||Brandon, you're not alone!!!  My '86 GT 4 speed is the same way...If I "hold" the shifter in reverse, I have backup lights, but as soon as I let go, the shifter slides off of the switch and they go out.  I had an '88 4 cyl. with the 5 speed and it didn't do it, I pretty much decided after looking at it that the design just sucked.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bill Osmer||11-17-2001||09:53 AM||||I've had the same situation - the cure: simply adjust the bolt that contact the reverse switch. Turn it about 1/4 of a turn at a time until your B/U lights stay on. (NOTE: too far will get them on when you're in 1st)<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||14
